 ## Bootstrap preservation boundary
 
+The kit belongs inside a dedicated project directory: `<project>/sds-dev-governance`.
+Never bootstrap directly into the user's HOME or the filesystem root, including physical
+aliases. Both `init.sh` and the metaprompt must explain this boundary; the shared engine
+rejects those targets before planning, copying files or invoking installers, even in dry-run
+and hub modes. Resolve the account's HOME as well as the environment's HOME. Existing kits
+in an unsafe location are not moved or deleted automatically.
+
 Bootstrap is file creation, never an upgrade or reconciliation of an existing kit.
 `--dry-run` computes the complete write plan; `--files-only` invokes no capability installer.
 Only newly generated files receive placeholder substitution or executable modes.
